{"event": "span_start", "trace_id": "trace_f33bb4f266734c4f955c5ed7490ac4cc", "span_id": "span_80331a8baa1d44eebde1f8f5", "parent_id": "span_cbcf7a32be1b4908bcf52c29", "type": "Generation", "depth": 3, "logged_at": "2026-08-13T10:37:52.501176+00:00"}
{"event": "span_end", "trace_id": "trace_f33bb4f266734c4f955c5ed7490ac4cc", "span_id": "span_1fec0fb50c734c9fbd67d6a9", "parent_id": "span_304a8a68b7a74854ac3da870", "type": "Function", "depth": 3, "duration": 3930.32, "detail": "\u2192 output: Summary:\nNigeria is advancing local production of armoured vehicles, including the AEGIS-X 2.0 and Vanquisher APCs, as part of its defence self-reliance strategy. The Defence Industries Corporation of Nigeria collaborates with local firms to meet military needs. The Africa International Defence Exhibition in Lagos showcases this progress.\n\nSources:\n\n\n        1.\n        Title: DICON X-Shield Unveils Light Tactical Armoured Vehicle AEGIS-X 2.0 * Military Africa\n        URL: https://www.military.africa/2026/08/dicon-x-shield-unveils-light-tactical-armoured-vehicle-aegis-x-2-0\n        Content:\n        ## The DICON X-Shield AEGIS-X 2.0 is an advanced, indigenously designed and manufactured Light Tactical Armoured Vehicle (LTAV) built in Nigeria. Officially unveiled in August 2026 under a strategic partnership between the Defence Industries Corporation of Nigeria (DICON) and X-Shield Solution Limited, it represents a significant milestone in Nigeria's pursuit of national defence self-reliance and technological sovereignty.\n\nMilitary Africa by Military Africa\n\nAugust 10, 2026\n\nin Defence Industry\n\nReading Time: 6 mins read [...] That partnership fits a pattern DICON has pursued deliberately since President Bola Tinubu signed the Defence Industries Corporation of Nigeria Act into law in November 2023. The legislation, sponsored by Babajimi Benson, Chairman of the House Committee on Defence, replaced DICON\u2019s original 1964 charter and gave the corporation new authority to form subsidiaries, take on private capital and enter joint ventures with local manufacturers. X-Shield is one of several private companies DICON has since paired with. The corporation\u2019s Command Engineering Depot produced the Ezugwu mine-resistant, ambush-protected vehicle in-house from 2019, Vanquish Industries Limited delivered 15 Vanquisher light armoured personnel carriers to the Nigerian Army in March 2026 under a similar arrangement, and [...] Army in March 2026 under a similar arrangement, and DICON\u2019s ", "logged_at": "2026-08-13T10:37:52.652148+00:00"}
{"event": "span_end", "trace_id": "trace_f33bb4f266734c4f955c5ed7490ac4cc", "span_id": "span_f493a5f3b3214e0aa05ae441", "parent_id": "span_71765509d46d46c783f71866", "type": "Function", "depth": 3, "duration": 4113.34, "detail": "\u2192 output: Summary:\nNigeria's Defence Industries Corporation partnered with EIB Group for military technology and production in 2026. EIB Group is the foreign partner for this joint venture. The deal aims to boost Nigeria's defense manufacturing capabilities.\n\nSources:\n\n\n        1.\n        Title: DICON Signs $2 Billion Defence Deal With SP Offshore Nigeria\n        URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ecjWiep9LPg\n        Content:\n        In a significant move to strengthen Nigeria's defense capabilities and reduce its reliance on foreign arms, the Defense Industries Corporation of Nigeria, DICON, has entered into a landmark $2 joint venture with SP Offshore Nigeria. The announcement was made in Kaduna by DICON's Director General, Major General Babachir Ibrahim Alyer, during the formal signing of a memorandum of understanding. He said the strategic partnership is aimed at building local manufacturing capacity and conserving foreign exchange, calling it a bold step towards national self-reliance in military production. Memorandum of understanding we are about to sign will take DICON to another level because we are going to partner with another Nigerian company to produce ammunition, weapon, where we can be producing fast [...] produce ammunition, weapon, where we can be producing fast assault crafts, security vehicles, and other platforms. So, it's a great day for DICON because this joint venture company we are going to form together will expedite the achievement of a military industrial complex and indigenous production. And we hope the partnership will take the defense defense industries to a greater heights uh whereby we'll be able to satisfy all the needs of the Nigerian armed forces and other security agencies in terms of weapons, ammunition, and other critical platforms. Chief Executive Officer of SP Offshore Nigeria, Mr. Obafemi Adekunle, stated that the collaboration will encourage defense-related investments, promote technology transfer, and generate employment opportuni", "logged_at": "2026-08-13T10:37:52.653147+00:00"}
