{"event": "span_end", "trace_id": "trace_f33bb4f266734c4f955c5ed7490ac4cc", "span_id": "span_dc8b9a39fa644737b3f01401", "parent_id": "span_252210af003341dbaab3a3b4", "type": "Function", "depth": 3, "duration": 3780.33, "detail": "\u2192 output: Summary:\nNigeria's Defence Industries Corporation (DICON) and private firms like Innoson and Imperium Industries are manufacturing armored vehicles locally to reduce reliance on imports. Efforts include technology transfer and partnerships to boost domestic production.\n\nSources:\n\n\n        1.\n        Title: Nigeria's evolving defence industry - Army Technology\n        URL: https://www.army-technology.com/analyst-comment/nigeria-evolving-defence-industry\n        Content:\n        Skip to site menu Skip to page content\n\nAT\n\n Analyst Comment\n\n# Nigeria\u2019s evolving defence industry\n\nNigerian-manufactured MRAPS and UAVs demonstrate the country\u2019s evolving defence industry. However, a reliance on the licensed production of foreign designs will continue.\n\nGlobaldata   GlobalData  April 7, 2026\n\nShare\n\n Copy Link\n Share on X\n Share on Linkedin\n Share on Facebook\n\nThe primary player in Nigeria\u2019s defence industry is state-owned DICON, itself run by the Nigerian Armed Forces. Credit: hyotographics via Shutterstock.com.\n\n### Unlock Free Access to Premium Content\n\n#### Discover exclusive forecasts, analyst insights and in-depth defence industry analysis.\n\nWith a free Army Technology profile, you can:\n        \n\n        2.\n        Title: DICON UNVEILS NIGERIAN-MADE ARMOURED ...\n        URL: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=T5M869QUTO0\n        Content:\n        # DICON UNVEILS NIGERIAN-MADE ARMOURED MILITARY VEHICLES\n## Arise News\n1230000 subscribers\n219 likes\n\n### Description\n14995 views\nPosted: 30 Jan 2026\nSubscribe to our Channel for high profile interviews. Follow us on Twitter at  | \nand Instagram:  | \nand Facebook:  |\n Check out our website www.arise.tv [...] of State for Defense says Nigeria is close to being self-sufficient in defense hardware. The vehicles which are we areing today reflects the depth of competence. It is designed for the realities of modern operations which include, mobility, protection, adaptability and survivability while remaining cost effective and suitable ", "logged_at": "2026-08-13T10:37:54.538327+00:00"}
